+### The repayment schedule, the egg prices, the funding card and the registrations card, 28 Oct 2026 (branch `feature/voice-assistant`, uncommitted when written)
+
+Four additions to the analysis, all Python and data with no model, a browser gate for the plan card and a test of where the model sits. After them the response has 10 top-level keys, the suite 2,177 tests in 58 files and the dictionaries 890 keys (7,120 values). The tables and the measured gate runs are in `docs/HACKATHON.md` §2.2 and §7; this entry holds the reasons.
+
+- **The repayment schedule** (`schedule_service.py`). Counted in whole paise so the columns add up to the card's totals: the payment is rounded to a whole rupee and the last one clears the remainder. The DSCR is the pressure ratio read the other way up, so it adds no new test and no lender's threshold is attached to it. `drive` checks the table to the paisa; `tools/README.md` lists its findings and the defects planted to prove it fires.
+- **The egg prices** (`necc_egg_prices.json`). NECC gave permission by e-mail; the owner's contact details stay out of the repo. The sheet prints whole numbers with no unit, so 640 is read as 640 paise an egg and the pages print NECC's own number beside the reading. NECC's `Average` column disagrees with its daily cells for Kolkata (632.59 against 634.46), so it is never read. 4 of the 34 centres are skipped (`tools/necc-crosswalk.json` gives each reason). A row without NECC's clarification is not drawn (`drawableMarketRows`). Editing `necc-lib.mjs` or `fetch-necc-prices.mjs` invalidates the data file's `script_sha256`, the same rule as the market fetch.
+- **The plan card's gate** (`talk-ui` S16 to S22). The card had Python tests and no browser test; the gate drives it in a real Edge against the fake model. It ended at 24 scenarios and 460 checks, and its 20 refuters are listed in the header of `talk-ui.mjs`.
+- **The funding card** (`structuring_service.py`, `components/SchemeFunding.jsx`). It prices only the schemes whose published terms give figures: PMEGP, PMFME and Mudra. Stand-Up India's period reads "upto 31.03.2025" with a successor announced in the 2025-26 Budget and its margin figures differ between sources, so it gets a status sentence and no sum.
+  - PMEGP is priced as a `general` and a `special` case because the app never asks for a social category. Asking would put age, gender and social category into every request, which changes `SENT_FIELDS`, fails parity4's notice check until `NOTICE_VERSION` is bumped and means re-translating 60 notice keys no native speaker has read. That is why the owner's age, gender and social category matcher was left out; the cost is that a reader sees both cases and reads their own.
+  - The subsidy base is capped at ₹20 lakh for everyone, the lower of PMEGP's two ceilings, so nobody is shown a larger subsidy than a rule gives them. A place that is neither `rural` nor `urban` gets the urban rates, the lower ones, with `area_assumed` printed.
+  - The reader's own money is a share of the whole project cost, as both schemes word it, and the net loan is the cost less that share and the subsidy. Mudra has no subsidy and no stated own share, so its `band` follows the funding gap (`none` at 0, `above_limit` past ₹20 lakh).
+  - Each source has a gap that the card prints as a caveat (`terms`): PMEGP's approval ran to 31 March 2026 and a continuation could not be confirmed; PMFME's page is about units that want to upgrade and is dated 10 Feb 2021; Mudra's food-processing match is our inference from "Non-agricultural". No eligibility rule is evaluated and the repayment is not tested against the household, so the net loan can exceed the safe-loan cards, which is why the card calls itself an estimate.
+  - Two traps. A typed `response_model` drops a key it does not declare, silently (the way `match_level` once disappeared), so `scheme_funding: dict` had to be added to `UnifiedAnalysisResponse` before the key reached a client. And the card's headings are scheme names, so `drive`'s scheme-card walk would have failed it for having no fit label; the walk leaves out `[data-scheme-funding]`. `SchemeFunding.jsx`'s `money` is a sixth copy of the page money formatters, on purpose.
+  - Measured on 28 Oct 2026 for UP / Lucknow, rural: tailoring and handicrafts 14 schemes in 6 tiers (funding for PMMY and PMEGP, 1 market row); food processing 18 in 6 (PMFME, PMMY, PMEGP); agriculture 11 in 5 tiers, all national, `no_scheme`, 3 mandi rows; poultry 15 in 5 tiers, all national so no fit chart, PMMY and PMEGP, 1 egg row.
+- **The registrations card** (`compliance_service.py`, `components/Compliance.jsx`). The owner asked for a step-by-step roadmap of the registrations (FSSAI, GST, Udyam) for the chosen sector. It is four steps in a fixed order (`udyam`, `local`, `fssai`, `gst`) and says only what a text that was read says; where none was read, it says to ask the office.
+  - **Sources**, all read on 28 Oct 2026: the FSSAI Licensing and Registration Regulations 2011 (Gazette of 1 Aug 2011) and FSSAI's compendium of 9 Nov 2017, the CBIC booklet "GST: An Update" of 1 June 2019, and the Udyam portal. `DATA_SOURCES.md` has the list and what is not said. The limits are constants beside a comment that names their source, because there are a handful and each needs its source next to it. The cost is that nothing re-checks them: they are the 2017 and 2019 figures, not checked against later amendments.
+  - **Wording the sources force.** `need` is never "required". FSSAI is "usually", because reg. 1.2.1(4) joins the sales and daily limits with "and/or". Exactly at a GST limit is `within`, because the booklet says registration is mandatory "only if the turnover exceeds" it. The booklet gives no rule for a business that sells both goods and services, so such a business is `mixed` and, between the two limits, gets `between` and "ask the office". It says nothing firm about a farmer's own produce, so the card says "can be treated differently" and asks. Tailoring is `mixed` on purpose: stitching for a customer is a service and selling garments is goods.
+  - **Its own word tables, never `CATEGORY_SYNONYMS`.** That map bridges wording for the scheme matcher and is documented as never widening eligibility (`dairy → poultry` exists so one button reaches one scheme); a registration rule that borrowed it would inherit mappings made for another purpose. Food words match whole words ("steam" holds "tea"); goods words match as substrings of the ten button values. A phrase typed under "other" that holds none of them, or is in a non-Latin script, comes out `mixed` for GST and `depends` for FSSAI, which only ever asks the reader to check.
+  - **No request field.** Yearly sales is `expected_monthly_revenue × 12`, worked out in `analysis_service.py`, so `SENT_FIELDS`, the notice and the log are unchanged. `udyam.schemes_requiring` counts the matched schemes whose eligibility line is "Udyam registration is required", which is only two (Kerala and North-East).
+  - **Traps.** The same silent drop as the funding card: `compliance: dict` had to be declared on `UnifiedAnalysisResponse`. `drive.mjs` restates the mapping itself (`complianceSteps`) and does not import the component's, so a wrong component fails the gate. A result stored before the card has no `compliance` key and the page must draw nothing and not throw, which the `old` pass of `drive` covers. `Compliance.jsx`'s `money` is a seventh copy of the page money formatters, on purpose.
+  - **How it was checked.** `test_compliance_service.py` (70 tests, every branch reached through `run_unified_analysis`) and 24 hand-made mutations of the service, each caught. Five defects planted in the card, singly and together, each made `drive` exit 1 with the finding meant for it (`tools/README.md` lists them); the 14 other browser gates were run once on the finished card.
+- **The registrations card on a phone.** A look at 390px in English showed "registration" cut in the middle: the title was `flex-1` (basis 0) beside a `shrink-0` badge, so the badge never dropped to its own line. The title now has a 9rem basis (`flex-[1_1_9rem]`). No gate measures a word split across two lines, so a one-off probe did, outside the repo: four requests (between them every badge and case), 8 languages, and three looks (390px at the normal text size, 360px and 320px at the largest). With `flex-1` put back it reports broken words in English at 390px; with the fix 88 of the 96 looks are clean. The other 8 are Malayalam at the largest text, where one word of up to 25 characters is wider than the card and breaks at its edge, as it does in the other cards on the same page, and, at 320px, which the gates do not cover (their floor is 360px), the journey label ("Step 3 of 4 · …") sticks out 17px. None of the three was changed.
+- **The model boundary** (`test_model_boundary.py`, 24 tests). "The analysis has no model" was a sentence, so the test makes the imports say it: a module under `services/` other than `intake_service` and `plan_service` imports neither the Meta client nor its ledger, nor those two services, nor a web framework, `importlib`, `subprocess`, `asyncio` or anything that opens a connection; the two helper services import nothing of ours but the schemas and each other; only `core/meta_client.py` opens a connection; only `main.py` and `smoke_meta.py` build the client; and a real `POST /api/analysis/run` on a helper-on app whose model records every call makes none and answers what a helper-off app answers. It closes the way in, not every way a value could depend on a model, so a new import fails it and has to be argued for on purpose. Twelve planted imports each failed it, and every file was put back byte for byte.
+- **Not built, and why.** A village- or block-level SWOT: the market data is district-level and the repo holds no census data, so it would claim more than the data backs. Growth assumptions: they would put a figure on screen that no source gives. WhatsApp and Bhashini: the web page is the channel and Muse Voice Transcribe does the speech step. Offline Llama models: every model call stays on Meta's cloud API under the spend cap, because the owner's laptop is personal and is not to become an AI server.
